ment’s decision meant that notes would not function as a means of payment, thus acting as a monetary reform that stabilized prices in terms of the newly circulating coins. Paper money would not circulate again in large amounts until the end of 1931.”'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2094, 'temperature': 0.2})
